WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:04.470
Over the last couple of years, India’s most underprivileged
 citizens have taken to the streets in thousands to

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:08.189
protest violence, government policies, and
to demand more rights.

00:00:08.189 --> 00:00:11.470
Hundreds of millions of people from the nation’s lowest 
caste will be a force to

00:00:11.470 --> 00:00:15.130
be reckoned with when they head to the polls
to vote in the national elections due by May.

00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:18.259
This is your Bloomberg QuickTake on Lower
Caste Political Power

00:00:18.259 --> 00:00:22.900
Hindus, which make up 80 percent of modern
India, were traditionally split into four

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:24.689
hierarchical groups.

00:00:24.689 --> 00:00:30.070
The lowest of all, Dalits, 
now form a quarter of the population, - about

00:00:30.070 --> 00:00:34.320
16 percent of all voters
On the ground, there is a lot of discontent,

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:36.050
especially amongst the Dalits.

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:51.620
One hopeful to replace Narendra Modi as prime
minister is is Mayawati -- a former Delhi

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:55.650
slum native who has been elected chief minister
of India’s most-populous state of Uttar

00:00:55.650 --> 00:00:57.420
Pradesh four times.

00:00:57.420 --> 00:01:02.270
Her party, Bahujan Samaj, vows to end caste
discrimination and build a society based on

00:01:02.270 --> 00:01:03.960
equality and fairness.

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:27.050
Laws against caste discrimination were adopted
seven decades ago, but with some exceptions

00:01:27.050 --> 00:01:31.470
caste remains a major factor in determining
how people earn a living and whom they marry,

00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:35.840
especially in the small towns and villages
where around 70% of Indians live.

00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:52.409
Modi rode a wave of dissatisfaction and emphasized
his own modest background to take power in

00:01:52.409 --> 00:01:58.450
2014, but his BJP party has developed a potentially
problematic reputation as far as Dalit voters

00:01:58.450 --> 00:02:01.479
are concerned.

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:20.030
Despite living in a stratified society where
circumstances of birth define a large part

00:02:20.030 --> 00:02:24.250
of what the future will hold, voters in the
world’s largest democracy will soon be hitting

00:02:24.250 --> 00:02:25.870
the polls as equals.

00:02:25.870 --> 00:02:29.090
Each political party will tailor its message
with that in mind.

